---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../lib/links';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Stylebot does with your data: no server, no account, no analytics."
>
  <main class="privacy">
    <div class="privacy-intro">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        Stylebot has no server, no account and no analytics. Your styles stay in
        your browser unless you turn on sync, chat or the command line, and then
        they go straight to a service you chose or an app you allowed.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated October 8, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Your styles, profiles, settings, history, chat conversations and API
        keys are saved in your browser's extension storage, and uninstalling
        Stylebot removes them. Stylebot reads the pages you visit to style
        them, and sends nothing from them unless you use chat or the command
        line.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google Drive sync</h2>
      <p>
        When you connect Google Drive in Options, your styles are saved to a
        file in your own Drive. Stylebot can only see the files it creates. Its
        access token stays in your browser and expires after an hour.
        Disconnect in Options or in your{' '}
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stylebot's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the{' '}
        <a
          href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
          >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
        >, including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Chat</h2>
      <p>
        When you add an API key and send a message, your browser sends it
        straight to that provider with your message, any screenshot you
        attach, the page's address and title, an outline of what's visible on
        the page, and its CSS and your styles. That can include personal
        information shown on the page, so don't use chat on pages you wouldn't
        share with the provider. Their policy applies:{' '}
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic</a>,{' '}
        <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI</a>,{' '}
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">Google</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Command line</h2>
      <p>
        When you turn on{' '}
        <q>Let apps on this computer control Stylebot</q> in Options, apps
        running as you can list your tabs, read pages, take screenshots, and
        read and change your styles, through a local connection only you can
        use. What they read can reach the services they use, such as the model
        behind a coding agent. Turn the setting off to disconnect.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fonts and imported CSS</h2>
      <p>
        Google Fonts in your styles are downloaded from Google, which sees your
        IP address. Stylesheets you <code>@import</code> are fetched from their
        address.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        stylebot.dev has no ads or cookies and is hosted on GitHub Pages, which
        keeps standard server logs. Plausible counts visits by page, referrer,
        country and device type, without cookies or anything that identifies
        you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Stylebot doesn't collect, sell or share your data. It only leaves your
        browser for the services above, when you use them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Changes to this policy are listed in the{' '}
        <a href={`${LINKS.github}/commits/v4/site/src/pages/privacy.astro`}
          >site's history on GitHub</a
        >. Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.feedbackEmail}`}
          >{LINKS.feedbackEmail}</a
        > or a <a href={LINKS.issues}>GitHub issue</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 0;
  }

  .privacy-intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font: 700 clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 48px) / 1.05 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .privacy-intro p {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .privacy-intro .updated {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  section {
    padding: 40px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font: 700 26px/1.2 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    font: 400 16px/1.65 var(--ui);
    color: var(--ink2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  code {
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--fill);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font: 400 0.88em/1.5 var(--mono);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .privacy {
      padding-top: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
